{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan","id":1446479,"title":"Changeling Lifespan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-29T12:45:41-07:00","id":1446479,"title":"Changeling Lifespan","content":"I had really enjoyed the concept of <b><i>Changeling: The Lost 1.5 </i></b>of a changeling character potentially becoming immortal. This connects to the conflict in the myth and folklore about the fae\u2019s longevity. The Irish saw the fae as truly immortal while the Scottish saw them as merely long lived. I am disappointed that <b><i>Changeling: The Lost 2</i></b> seems to be moving away from this. Not because I simply want to play a high wyrd immortal changeling character, but because I want to play major folklore and fairytale heroes and villains as major NPC characters. I want to introduce Titania as the founder of the Spring court, Morgana Ley Fey and Nimue as two of the original members of the Autumn Court, Mordred as the tragically heroic Winter king of the Brittish Isles, Koschei the Deathless as the monarch of the Night Court, and Vasilisa the Beautiful as the Queen of the Day Court. I want to introduce them as characters that can help or hinder a changeling motley. That they could be either hero or villain depending on their mood.<br /> <br /> What I have set up in my chronicles is that starting on wyrd 7, the Changeling\u2019s lifespan is greatly increased and a changeling becomes nearly immortal at wyrd 10<br /> <br /> Wyrd 7 +150 years to changeling\u2019s lifespan<br /> Wyrd 8 + 300 years to changeling\u2019s lifespan<br /> Wyrd 9 +600 years to changeling\u2019s lifespan<br /> Wyrd 10 the changeling is immune to the effects/ penalties of aging, disease, and drugs. The Changeling is also more fantasy and dream than mortal flesh at this point. With the exception of their frailties and cold iron, the changeling only takes damage from supernatural attacks, which includes the base attacks of changelings/fae/ hobgoblins.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T13:36:41-07:00","id":1446489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan#post1446479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had really enjoyed the concept of <b><i>Changeling: The Lost 1.5 </i></b>of a changeling character potentially becoming immortal. This connects to the conflict in the myth and folklore about the fae\u2019s longevity. The Irish saw the fae as truly immortal while the Scottish saw them as merely long lived. I am disappointed that <b><i>Changeling: The Lost 2</i></b> seems to be moving away from this. Not because I simply want to play a high wyrd immortal changeling character, but because I want to play major folklore and fairytale heroes and villains as major NPC characters. I want to introduce Titania as the founder of the Spring court, Morgana Ley Fey and Nimue as two of the original members of the Autumn Court, Mordred as the tragically heroic Winter king of the Brittish Isles, Koschei the Deathless as the monarch of the Night Court, and Vasilisa the Beautiful as the Queen of the Day Court. I want to introduce them as characters that can help or hinder a changeling motley. That they could be either hero or villain depending on their mood.<br /> <br /> What I have set up in my chronicles is that starting on wyrd 7, the Changeling\u2019s lifespan is greatly increased and a changeling becomes nearly immortal at wyrd 10<br /> <br /> Wyrd 7 +150 years to changeling\u2019s lifespan<br /> Wyrd 8 + 300 years to changeling\u2019s lifespan<br /> Wyrd 9 +600 years to changeling\u2019s lifespan<br /> Wyrd 10 the changeling is immune to the effects/ penalties of aging, disease, and drugs. The Changeling is also more fantasy and dream than mortal flesh at this point. With the exception of their frailties and cold iron, the changeling only takes damage from supernatural attacks, which includes the base attacks of changelings/fae/ hobgoblins.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are still ways for Changelings to achieve Immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T14:58:31-07:00","id":1446498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan?p=1446489#post1446489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are still ways for Changelings to achieve Immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I not only want them to be immortal, but also the pagan gods and sidhe of myth whose perspectives and powers are no longer truly mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T15:10:20-07:00","id":1446505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan?p=1446489#post1446489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are still ways for Changelings to achieve Immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember how <i><b>Oberon </b></i>and <i><b>Titania </b></i>are portrayed in the old Disney cartoon<i><b>, Gargoyles</b></i>(1994-1997)? That is a source of inspiration for how the characters can potentially be portrayed in a changeling chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T08:10:12-07:00","id":1446980,"title":"","content":"Changlings still get +20 years per dot of Wyrd added to their lifespan. That's +100 years ay Wyd 5 and +200 years at Wyrd 10.<br /> <br /> The examples you're pulling? Those would be Gentry Titles, not Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T10:53:43-07:00","id":1447000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan?p=1446980#post1446980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changlings still get +20 years per dot of Wyrd added to their lifespan. That's +100 years ay Wyd 5 and +200 years at Wyrd 10.<br /> <br /> The examples you're pulling? Those would be Gentry Titles, not Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to their personalities. That is, they genuinely like mortals and want to do what is best for them. However, they are so powerful and arrogant that this can put them in antagonistic positions at times.<br /> <br /> Also, several famous fairytale characters I want to introduce as high wyrd changelings are over 200 years old. That would require them to live more than 300 years.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T11:05:24-07:00","id":1447001,"title":"","content":"On the official Gargoyles forum, one of the series creators, Greg Weisman emphasized that Oberon loves mortals and several of the actions; including his law of non-interference and attempt to take Alexander Xanatos back to Avalon was done out of a desire what he thought was best for mortals/the baby. And that puck genuinly loves Alexander Xanatos as a son or favored nephew and has genuine bonds of loyalty to David Xanatos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T12:15:03-07:00","id":1447014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan?p=1447001#post1447001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the official Gargoyles forum, one of the series creators, Greg Weisman emphasized that Oberon loves mortals and several of the actions; including his law of non-interference and attempt to take Alexander Xanatos back to Avalon was done out of a desire what he thought was best for mortals/the baby. And that puck genuinly loves Alexander Xanatos as a son or favored nephew and has genuine bonds of loyalty to David Xanatos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gentry are often portrayed as selfish, but they can just as well have the best of intentions when they steal someone away from the mortal world. A Keeper who loves humanity might take mortals to bring some much needed humanity to their domain, and a Keeper who falls in love with a human would definitely abduct them in order to keep them safe in Arcadia where they can dote on them and guard them. The damage comes from how alien they are from humanity; not beholden to any form of morality we could recognise and truly unable to understand what's actually best for humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:19:41-07:00","id":1447043,"title":"","content":"Note: Oberon past the law of non-interference to stop <i>The Children of Oberon</i>(The name of his race) from casually interfering in the lives of mortals. Alexander Xanatos is 1/4 <i>Child of Oberon</i> and his wife's grandchild. However, one Goliath showed him there was a better way, he took it.<br /> <br /> Also, from my understanding of True Fae, they can't feel emotions of love, gratitude, or genuine friendship, though they can mimic these emotions. They can feel feelings of obligation, but it is often in regard to turning in a favor or obligation he owes the changeling/mortal. <i>Sebastien</i> from <b><i>Black Butler </i></b>I think it a good example of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T17:05:56-07:00","id":1447058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan?p=1447014#post1447014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gentry are often portrayed as selfish, but they can just as well have the best of intentions when they steal someone away from the mortal world. A Keeper who loves humanity might take mortals to bring some much needed humanity to their domain, and a Keeper who falls in love with a human would definitely abduct them in order to keep them safe in Arcadia where they can dote on them and guard them. T.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just want to say that I really LIKE/LOVE this idea, and wish it worked better with my understanding of the Gentry. I do plan to use this idea in some of my plans for the Gentry. Would that be okay?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T23:19:24-07:00","id":1447119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan?p=1447058#post1447058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just want to say that I really LIKE/LOVE this idea, and wish it worked better with my understanding of the Gentry. I do plan to use this idea in some of my plans for the Gentry. Would that be okay?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T12:14:54-07:00","id":1447243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446479-changeling-lifespan?p=1447058#post1447058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just want to say that I really LIKE/LOVE this idea, and wish it worked better with my understanding of the Gentry. I do plan to use this idea in some of my plans for the Gentry. Would that be okay?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a vast difference between &quot;this is how I will run it in my game&quot; vs. &quot;This is what the official source says on the matter.&quot; You don't need anyone's permission to run it any way you like, but you might want to inform players that things they might know about the setting as written are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}